  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Find the fifth term of the sequence given by the recurrence relation\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=2{a}_{n-1}-3,\\,{a}_{1}=5,\\,n\\ge 2.\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Starting with the first term ${a}_{1}=5,$ we compute the next terms using the recursive formula until we reach the fifth term.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =5 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =2{a}_{1}-3=2\\cdot 5-3=7 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =2{a}_{2}-3=2\\cdot 7-3=11 \\\\ {a}_{4} & =2{a}_{3}-3=2\\cdot 11-3=19 \\\\ {a}_{5} & =2{a}_{4}-3=2\\cdot 19-3=35\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fifth term is ${a}_{5}=35.$",
